        "id": 148629,
        "name": "Honolulu Blue",
        "username": "Honolulu_Blue",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/ecae2f/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-09-23T22:24:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"ogseamus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ogseamus/48/4830_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ogseamus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I wanted to start a thread to make some challenging scenarios for people to play in the video game. I think it is even more fun now with multiplayer (even though I am still waiting on my tablet).I was wondering if people had any really good ideas for fun and/or challenging games.</p>\n<p><strong>Leaders of Men</strong></p>\n<p>Leaders of Teams come together to stop a Leader in a showdownCitizen Dawn vs Legacy, DW Expat, AA in Silver Gulch</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I beat this one!&nbsp; It was surprisingly easy too, though neither Dawn nor SG threw the really bad cards at me.&nbsp; The surprise MVP was Argy's Scherzo of Frost and Flame, which I almost never use, but used to great effect here - doing 3+3 damage most turns (Galvanize and there was an Explosives Wagon in play).&nbsp; It was, indeed, the kill shot.</p>",
